From: radiance-web EnergyPlus WASM port
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] third_party/ssc: add missing <cstdint> include

What: adds `#include <cstdint>` to lib_battery_dispatch.cpp.

Why (toolchain, not physics): the file uses SIZE_MAX, which older glibc/libstdc++
transitively pulled in via other headers. gcc >= 15 (and Emscripten's clang-based
toolchain) no longer guarantees that transitive include, so the file fails to
compile with "SIZE_MAX was not declared in this scope" unless <cstdint> is
included directly. Pure header hygiene -- no code path or numerical behavior
changes.

Applies to: energyplus-src/third_party/ssc/shared/lib_battery_dispatch.cpp
Apply with (-p1, from the pristine energyplus-src/ tree root):
  patch -p1 < patches/energyplus/0001-cstdint-include-lib_battery_dispatch.patch

--- a/third_party/ssc/shared/lib_battery_dispatch.cpp
+++ b/third_party/ssc/shared/lib_battery_dispatch.cpp
@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@
 #include "lib_shared_inverter.h"
 
 #include <math.h>
+#include <cstdint> /* SIZE_MAX not transitively included with gcc>=15 */
 #include <algorithm>
 
